    "text": "<p>It is Haloform reaction.&nbsp;The haloform reaction is the reaction of a methyl ketone with chlorine, bromine, or iodine in the presence of hydroxide ions to give a carboxylate ion and a haloform.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0652cbe8-eee0-4553-a8bb-7b965fdcd9a5-image.png\" style=\"width: 650px; height: 157px;\" /></p>",
